<p>This is a decent skip. Your tone is spot on on most places, though in the first part of the description I would recommend referring to it as SCP-3042 rather than dog. In the researcher's note, removing the 'in all cases' on the end would make it a bit smoother to read. In fact, you could probably just say SCP-3042-1 instead of writing out 'the individual SCP-3042 is showing affection to'. Apart from those, your tone is excellent and I haven't noticed any spelling or grammar mistakes. The SCP itself is interesting. Though the 'invincible' thing is hard to pull of, I feel like you've done an acceptable job of it. The testing logs seem a bit redundant and could probably be shortened. All they do is show that it can break through anything and can't be injured, which I feel could be done just as effectively with fewer logs.</p>
